A Key is used to uniquely identify a Widget among its siblings, so Flutter can correctly preserve/match the corresponding Element and State when the widget tree changes.

Example
Column(
  children: [
    Text("A", key: ValueKey(1)),
    Text("B", key: ValueKey(2)),
  ],
)

If the order changes, the keys help Flutter understand:

“This is the same widget/state as before, just in a different position.”

Interview answer

“Keys uniquely identify widgets among their siblings and help Flutter preserve and correctly match their state when the widget tree changes.”

